Z||000000||sjp777||05-25-2001||08:38 PM||||I just saw the home video on the news of that wedding reception in Israel where the dance floor collapsed. Hundreds of people dancing, smiling and kissing, then they just disappear before your eyes.<P>Probably the most disturbing piece of video I have ever seen.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||11
Z||000001||Jay||05-25-2001||09:35 PM||||That was disturbing.  Could you imagine your wedding being marred by that?  What a way to start off!  What disturbed me just as much was Israel attacking Palestinian houses and killing a deaf kid who couldn't hear what was going on.  Granted it is a complicated issue over the land of Palestine, but baricading Palestinians into tiny areas and forcing them to work for the Jewish settlers because there is no infastructure is asking for problems.  I sympathize with all victims of this conflict, both the innocent Jews who are victims of suicide bombings and the Palestinians who have suffered from Israeli army attacks.  It is senseless violence that shows how sick this world has become.  Each side claims that the other is inhuman, after all how can humans kill children?  When Palestinians bomb they are called terrorists, when the Israelis attack they say it is self defense. The reality is that they are both cowardly acts of sensless violece.  This conflict can't be resolved by humans.  Even though the wedding disaster was not blamed on a bomb but rather on faulty construction, it is a symbol of what the Holy land is going through.  Both fighting in the name of God, and really doing a diservice to both their religion, nationality and the human race as a whole.  Just my 2 cents.  <P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande||||reg||1
