Z||000003||Taijiguy||05-25-2001||11:14 PM||||I just saw that video too. It is very disturbing. I always have mixed emotions when I see something like that. First is shock, and great sympathy for the victims. Then there's my own immediate sense of gratitude that I'm not so desensitized that things like that don't bother me. <BR>That was a sad occurrence.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierospeeder||05-25-2001||11:54 PM||||I taped it, so i can show my g/f.<P>I seen it yesterday on tv and i still like watching it.  Its just weird.  Just seeing people falling.  If anyone seen faces of death, its a video of people dying, there is one where an orchestra stage just collapses and people die.<P>I sometimes have a fear of heights, i love flying and i feel safe in planes.  But i dont feel safe in buildings.  And just like a dog, you try to stay low to the ground like they do when something scares them.  I had a dream just like that where a floor collapses on me.<P>I heard 3 people got arrested, the builder, archtitect (SP) and someone else.  It was remodeled to have a bigger dance floor.  When i was taping this, it was on ABC and at the end he was saying that the baby that was seen being videotaped survived the fall.  <P>Best Wishes to the family members.||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||05-27-2001||07:27 AM||||i saw on this mornings news, they arrested the contractors who had remodeled the building, removed some of the columns supporting the floor under it to make the room under it more open. Oops.<P>we had the same thing happen in Ohio last summer at Put-In-Bay on Lake Erie. Concrete dance floor caved in at Lonz Winery. I think only one was killed there.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 05-27-2001).]||||reg||1
